 "notes": "MiniBooNE dump-mode constraints on ALP-photon coupling extracted from Fig. 7 (2\u03c3 C.L.). The paper presents new laboratory limits on g_agamma for masses below ~100 keV, extending previous astrophysical constraints from HB stars and SN1987a. Data points are approximate readings from the exclusion contour in Fig. 7. The paper also discusses ArgoNeuT projections (shown as benchmark signal rates of 3, 20, 100 events) but these are not actual measured limits, only sensitivity projections without dedicated analysis. The AxionPhoton coupling type is appropriate as the paper constrains g_agamma (axion-photon coupling) via production and detection channels involving photons and electromagnetic cascades in the beam dump. | vector-trace candidate: MB_ARGONEUT_limits2sigma.pdf colour (0.86, 0.08, 0.24), 316 pts (selected among 10) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 316))",
